WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.173 --> 00:00:01.006
- I was very nervous,

00:00:01.006 --> 00:00:03.050
I was like, "I wanna say his name right."

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.050
I love the German language.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:04.960
- Yeah, but the last name is-

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.170
- Schweighofer.
- Schweighofer is fantastic.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.010
And the last name is like,

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:11.363
even for my family,
sometimes unpronounceable.

00:00:11.363 --> 00:00:12.420
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.230
- Is that after alcohol is involved?

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:15.291
- Yeah, after a lot of alcohol.

00:00:15.291 --> 00:00:16.732
It's like
(mumbling)

00:00:16.732 --> 00:00:18.370
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.830
- That's probably how most
Americans sound when they say it.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.700
Well meet Jamie, have
y'all ever met before?

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:23.730
- Very nice to meet you.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.610
- I'm a huge fan of both
of you and it's crazy.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:31.280
Today everyone in Germany
was like, "Hug everyone."

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:32.680
It's crazy.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:33.513
- I love it.

00:00:33.513 --> 00:00:37.040
Well, "Army of Thieves" looks
great and funny as well.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.850
So did you direct this one?
Is that what I hear?

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.470
- Yes, I directed this movie.
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:43.750
- Yeah, because we did "Army Of The Dead",

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.170
and then at that time, my
character in that film,

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:51.824
it's name is Ludwig Dieter,
the Safe Cracker and...

00:00:51.824 --> 00:00:52.845
(audience cheering)

00:00:52.845 --> 00:00:53.678
- Very mysterious.

00:00:53.678 --> 00:00:55.210
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.487
(Kelly clapping and laughing)

00:00:57.487 --> 00:00:58.570
I am amazing.

00:00:59.646 --> 00:01:00.479
- I am.

00:01:00.479 --> 00:01:04.307
And one day Zack Snyder
called me and said,

00:01:04.307 --> 00:01:05.380
"Matthias, we have an idea

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:07.790
for a potential spinoff for the character,

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.620
so would you direct the film?"

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.820
And I said, "Yes, but
who's the character?"

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.710
And he said, "It's Dieter."

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.170
And I said.
- Oh, my gosh.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:16.355
- Thank God.

00:01:16.355 --> 00:01:17.276
(audience cheering)
- That's so cool.

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:18.750
- [Mathias] I left there
clapping all the way.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.250
- Are you getting recognized
everywhere right now?

00:01:22.361 --> 00:01:23.262
(Mathias speaking foreign language)

00:01:23.262 --> 00:01:26.290
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:29.553
- When there are Germans involved, a lot.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.933
There's a restaurant I love here in LA.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.097
Can I tell the story?

00:01:36.097 --> 00:01:37.590
- Yeah.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.320
- I was in a restaurant,
it was super relaxed

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.550
and I had breakfast and they were like

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:44.880
a group of people looking at me, you know?

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.144
And I thought, Americans,
they know me, that's cool.

00:01:49.144 --> 00:01:51.170
- Oh, my God, this is my moment.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.820
- Yeah, but after a few seconds,

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.570
I recognized, okay no, they're Germans.

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:58.620
And then when they saw
me recognizing them,

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.587
they thought like, okay,
let's go over there.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:03.710
"Can we have an autograph or a picture?"

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:04.740
So I took a picture

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.010
in front of all the other
Americans in the cafe.

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:10.210
But as you watch their faces,
it's like, "Who is he?"

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.767
(Kelly laughing)
(audience laughing)

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:13.651
"Who is this guy?"

00:02:13.651 --> 00:02:15.359
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:02:15.359 --> 00:02:16.500
- [Jamie] They're gonna know soon.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.730
- I love that though.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.180
You find your people
wherever you go though.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.470
I feel that about Texans.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:21.980
I'm from Texas here and everywhere I go,

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:22.870
even if you don't know each other,

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.291
you're like, "You're from Texas?"

00:02:24.291 --> 00:02:25.357
You don't even know each other,

00:02:25.357 --> 00:02:27.760
but you're like, "We're so similar."

